text Fuko is giving out her carvings today, too.
text The third-year students are the same as always. But others, especially the first-year female students, seem very happy to receive the starfish.
text When Fuko's handing out the carvings alone, {$lnmA} comes to her side to share her happiness.
text And right behind the ladies, Sunohara and I tag along to tease them...
text This has become our daily ritual.
text However, sometimes, there is this feeling of uncertainty inside me.
text Is our being by Fuko's side really for her sake?
text All we can do is to watch her.
text And at times, our presence may even disturb her.
text Is there really a meaning to our being here by her side?
text I share my thought with {$lnmA}.
